# Build-context exclusions for `podman build` / `docker build`.
#
# Honoured by both engines (podman also reads .containerignore; this
# file covers both since podman falls back to .dockerignore).
#
# Without this the context is ~1.3 GB — dist/ alone holds the previous
# PyInstaller ELFs (~340 MB) and a virtualenv another ~315 MB, none of
# which any Dockerfile needs.
#
# NOTE: build/ is NOT excluded wholesale — Dockerfile.build copies the
# source tree and PyInstaller needs build/axross.spec. Only the heavy,
# regenerable artifacts under it are dropped.

# Every hidden top-level entry: VCS metadata, virtualenvs, editor and
# tooling scratch dirs, local agent/control-plane state, cache dirs,
# dotenv files. None of it is needed to build or test (no Dockerfile or
# test reads a dot-path), and some of it is large or private — it must
# never be sent as build context, let alone baked into an image layer
# by `COPY . .`.
#
# Deliberately a wildcard rather than an enumerated list: a new hidden
# directory appearing in a working tree is then excluded by default,
# instead of being shipped until someone remembers to add it.
.*

venv/
env/

dist/
build-tmp/
build/appimagetool-*.AppImage
build/__pycache__/
**/__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/

htmlcov/
security/reports/
security/scanner_reports/

# Secrets must never enter a build context — a COPY . would bake them
# into an image layer that survives even if a later step deletes them.
# (Dotfile forms such as .env are already covered by the `.*` rule
# above; these catch the non-hidden spellings.)
*.key
*.pem
*.pfx
*.p12
*_token.json
*.sqlite
*.sqlite3
*.db

*.log
:memory:
